# System architecture & TypeScript

## 1. Language & localization (strict)
- **Code:** Source (variables, functions, interfaces, file names, Git commits, code comments) MUST be English.
- **UI:** All user-visible frontend text MUST be German — labels, buttons, headings, placeholders, tooltips, toasts, empty states. English library defaults must never reach the user.
- **Errors:** User-facing validation and error messages MUST be German.
- **Dates & numbers:** Display/input with `de-DE` (`tt.mm.jjjj`, 24h `HH:mm`, decimal `,`). Prefer custom fields over native `type="date"` / `type="number"` / `type="time"`.

## 2. Tech stack
- **Framework:** Next.js App Router; default to React Server Components.
- **Language:** TypeScript strict mode.
- **Database & auth:** Supabase (PostgreSQL + RLS). App schema: `leseno`.
- **UI:** Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui (when added), Lucide icons.
- **Validation:** Zod schemas; import `@/lib/validations/configure-zod` as side effect; explicit German messages per field.
- **Deploy:** GitHub → Coolify (Node 22). Secrets only via env (never commit `.env*`).

## 3. Structure
- App Router under `src/app/`
- Base UI: `@/components/ui/`
- Features: `@/components/features/`
- Shared logic: `@/lib/`
- No `any` — explicit types for props, actions, DB rows.
- `'use client'` only when state or browser events are required.

## 4. Server Actions
- Mutations via Server Actions + Zod.
- Return shape: `{ success: boolean; data?: T; error?: string }` (`ActionResult`).
